---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import { links } from '../config/links';

const title = 'Member participation code';
const lead =
  'The shared standards that keep the Society a genuine cross-disciplinary forum, where practitioners from very different backgrounds can exchange ideas honestly and respectfully.';
---

<Page title={title} eyebrow="Governance" lead={lead}>
  <Callout tone="pending" title="Draft">
    <p>
      This code is a draft, for adoption at the Society's first general meeting. It will be reviewed
      by the committee within two years of adoption.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <p class="lead">
    The code applies to members' participation in the Society's activities — meetings, online forums,
    events, publications and committee work. It does not regulate members' professional work outside
    the Society, though it reflects the standards the profession aspires to. When you join the
    Society, you agree to abide by it.
  </p>

  <p class="text-small text-muted">
    It is called a <em>participation code</em> because that is what it currently is. If professional
    certification is later introduced, a wider professional code may be required.
  </p>

  <h2>Professional integrity</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Be honest and accurate in contributions to the Society's forums, events and publications,
      including about data, methods, assumptions and the limits of what accounts can show.
    </li>
    <li>
      Represent your qualifications, experience and affiliations truthfully, and do not claim the
      Society's endorsement of your views, services or products.
    </li>
    <li>Acknowledge the work of others and respect intellectual property.</li>
    <li>
      Support good practice in natural capital accounting, anchored in the
      {' '}<a href={links.seea} rel="noopener">UN System of Environmental-Economic Accounting</a> and
      other relevant standards, while engaging openly with methodological debate.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Respect for others</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Treat other members and participants with courtesy and respect. Harassment, bullying and
      discrimination have no place in the Society's activities, online or in person.
    </li>
    <li>
      Debate ideas vigorously and people kindly: criticise methods and evidence, not individuals. The
      Society exists to exchange ideas and experience across disciplines — accountants, ecologists,
      economists, statisticians and policy-makers — and that only works if every discipline is heard
      with respect.
    </li>
    <li>Welcome newcomers and early-career members; share knowledge generously.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Acting in the Society's interests</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Participate as an individual, not as a representative of your employer or clients, unless
      expressly stated otherwise.
    </li>
    <li>
      Declare conflicts of interest where they arise in Society roles — committee decisions,
      reviewing papers, organising events or commissioning work — and step back where appropriate.
    </li>
    <li>Do not present personal views as positions of the Society unless authorised.</li>
    <li>Respect information shared in confidence in Society roles.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Upholding the code</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Concerns about conduct may be raised with the Secretary or President and will be handled by the
      committee fairly, confidentially and in accordance with the association's rules.
    </li>
    <li>
      Serious or repeated breaches may lead to action under the rules, including suspension or
      termination of membership.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <Callout tone="pending" title="Still to be settled">
    <p>
      A fuller enforcement pathway is being drafted: how to raise a concern and who receives
      complaints; how conflicts of interest are managed; what procedural fairness applies; the
      possible outcomes or sanctions; and whether there is an appeal process.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Raising a concern</h2>
  <p>
    If something in the Society's activities has fallen short of this code, tell us. Concerns are
    treated confidentially.
  </p>
  <p>
    <Cta href={links.complaints} variant="primary">Raise a concern</Cta>
  </p>
  <p>
    <Cta href="/complaints/" variant="arrow">How complaints are handled</Cta>
  </p>

  <hr />

  <p class="text-small text-muted">
    Adopted: at the first general meeting (date to be set). To be reviewed by the committee within
    two years of adoption.
  </p>
</Page>
